What is the role of RNA polymerase in the process of transcription and how does it differ from the role of DNA polymerase in replication?,"<bos><start_of_turn>user
What is the role of RNA polymerase in the process of transcription and how does it differ from the role of DNA polymerase in replication?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","RNA polymerase is a key enzyme in the process of transcription, which is the process of synthesizing RNA from a DNA template. DNA polymerase, on the other hand, is involved in replication, which is the synthesis of DNA from a DNA template.

In the process of transcription, RNA polymerase plays a crucial role in the following ways:
