1. Convert the child's weight to kilograms:  
   \[
   \text{Weight in kg} = \frac{32 \text{ lb}}{2.2 \text{ lb/kg}} = 14.5 \text{ kg}
   \]  
2. Calculate the total loading dose:  
   \[
   \text{Dose} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.5 \text{ kg} = 290 \text{ mg}
   \]  
3. Calculate the infusion time:  
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{290 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 580 \text{ min}
   \]  
   The dose should be administered over $\boxed{580 \text{ minutes}}$.
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

