The **principal constituents of Althaea (Marshmallow)** are **mucilage (80-90%)**, which includes pectinic acid and starch, along with saponins, tannins, flavonoids, and trace amounts of essential oils and minerals. The mucilage is responsible for its demulcent and soothing effects.",relevance,"# Task Description
