"A sphere of mass \( m \) and radius \( R \) is rolling without slipping on a horizontal surface with an initial velocity \( v_0 \). If the sphere is subject to a constant acceleration \( a \), what is the velocity of the sphere after a time \( t \)?","<bos><start_of_turn>user
A sphere of mass \( m \) and radius \( R \) is rolling without slipping on a horizontal surface with an initial velocity \( v_0 \). If the sphere is subject to a constant acceleration \( a \), what is the velocity of the sphere after a time \( t \)?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","To determine the velocity of the sphere after time \( t\), we analyze the translational and rotational components of the motion. Since the sphere is rolling without slipping, the translational velocity \( v_0 \) and the rotational velocity \( \omega \) are related by \( v_0 = R\omega \).

1. Translational motion:
The translational motion is given by the equation \( v_t = v_0 + a t \), where \( v_t \) is the translational velocity after time \( t \).

2. Rotational motion:
The rotational motion is given by the equation \( \omega = \omega_0 + \frac{1}{2} \alpha t \), where \( \omega \) is the angular velocity after time \( t \), and \( \alpha \) is the angular acceleration.

Since the sphere is rolling without slipping, the angular velocity is given by \( \omega = \frac{v_t}{R} \).
The initial angular velocity is \( \omega_0 = \frac{v_0}{R} \).

