   - The twist-boat form of cyclohexane is a conformation where the two carbonyl groups (if cyclohexane is a cyclic ketone) or the two hydrogen atoms at the ends of the ring are trans to each other.  
   - This form is more stable than the boat form due to reduced steric repulsion.  
   - The dihedral angle between the two ends is 45° (in cyclohexane).  

