   - The resulting ring in twistane is a highly strained, twisted cyclohexane ring.  
   - The dihedral angle between the two ends of the ring is 90°, making it a ""twist"" conformation.  
   - The twist-boat form of cyclohexane is a precursor to this twist-boat conformation, as the ring must adopt a twist-boat conformation before the cyclization can occur.  

