   - Derivatives of twistane are formed by modifying the substituents at the two ends of the ring.  
   - The dihedral angle between the two ends remains 90°, but the substituents can be chiral or achiral, depending on their structure.  
   - The stability and reactivity of twistane derivatives depend on the nature of the substituents and their electronic effects.  

