","To calculate the standard enthalpy change for the reaction:  
\[ \text{Fe(H}_2\text{O)}_6^{2+} + 2\text{Cl}^- \rightarrow \text{FeCl}_4^{2-} + 6\text{H}_2\text{O} \]  
We use the principle of Hess's law, which states that the enthalpy change for a reaction is the difference between the enthalpy change of the products and the enthalpy change of the reactants.  
The enthalpy change for the reaction can be calculated as:  
\[ \Delta H = \Delta H_{\text{products}} - \Delta H_{\text{products}} \]  
The enthalpy change for the formation of the complex ion \([FeCl_4]^{2-}\) is given as \(\Delta H_{\text{formation}} = -392\,\text{kJ/mol}\).  
The enthalpies of hydration for \(\text{Fe}^{2+}\) and \(\text{Cl}^-\) are \(\Delta H_{\text{hydr}} = -340\,\text{kJ/mol}\) and \(\Delta H_{\text{hydr}} = -381\,\text{kJ/mol}\), respectively.  

The enthalpy change for the formation of \([\text{Fe(H}_2\text{O}_6\text{)}^{\rightleftharpoons} + 6\text{H}_2\text{O}\).  
The enthalpy change for the hydrolysis of \(\text{Fe(H}_2\text{O}_6^{2+}\) is \(\Delta H_{\text{hydr}} = -340\,\text{K}\text{J/mol}\).  
The enthalpy change for the hydration of \(2\text{Cl}^-\) is \(2 \times (-381\,\text{kJ/mol}) = -762\,\text{kJ/mol}\).  

The enthalpy change for the formation of \([\text{Fe(H}_2\text{O}_6\text{}^2+\) is \(\Delta H_{\text{form}} = 0\) (since it is the reference for enthalpy of formation).  
The enthalpy change for the formation of \(\text{Fe(H}_2\text{O}_6^{2+}\) is \(\Delta H_{\text{hydr}} = -340\,\text{kJ/mol}\).  
The enthalpy change for the formation of \(2\text{Cl}^-\) is \(\Delta H_{\text{hydr}} = 2 \times -381\,\text{kJ/mol} = -762\,\text{kJ/mol}\).  

The enthalpy change for the formation of \([\text{Fe(H}_2\text{O}_6\text{}^2+}\) and \(2\text{Cl}^-\) is:  
