   \[
   \text{Weight of nitrogen and other gases} = 250 \, \text{g} \times 0.77 = 192.5 \, \text{g}
   \]
   The oxygen is consumed, and sulphur is added, so the weight of the residual gases is:
   \[
   \text{Weight of residual gases} = 192.5 \, \text{g} + 58 \, \text{g} = 250 \, \text{g} - 57.5 \, \text{g} = 192.5 \, \text{g} + 58 \, \text{g} - 57.5 \, \text{g} = 1
