\[
1.2 \times 10^{20} = \frac{x}{(1)(0.25)^6}
\]
\[
x = 1.2 \times 10^{20} \times (0.25)^6 = 1.2 \times 10^{20} \times 1.44 \times 10^{-4.6} = 1.6 \times 10^{15}
\]
However, this value is too large, as the concentration of Fe\(^3^+$ is 1.0 M, and \(x\) cannot exceed this value. Since the equilibrium constant is very large, the reaction will proceed almost completely to completion. Thus, the concentration of Fe\(^3^+$ will be very small, and the concentration of CN\(^-\) will be much larger than 0.25 M.

