   - **DNA conformation**: The accessibility of the DNA to the dMTase is critical. If the DNA is tightly bound to other proteins (e.g., histone complexes), dMTase may not be able to access the methylated cytosines.
   - **Chromatin accessibility**: The overall chromatin state (open or closed) plays a significant role. Open chromatin regions are more accessible to the MBD2/dMTase complex, while closed chromatin restricts access.

