","A space group is a mathematical description of the symmetry elements that can be applied to a crystal structure, ensuring that the structure remains unchanged. It is the mathematical basis for understanding the symmetry of crystal structures. The symmetry elements include rotations, reflections, and translations, which can be combined to generate the entire crystal structure.  

For example, if you rotate a crystal by 90 degrees and it looks the same, the crystal has a 90-degree rotation symmetry element. If you flip a crystal through a plane and it looks the same, it has a reflection symmetry element.  

Thus, a space group is a mathematical description of all possible symmetry operations that can be applied to a crystal structure without changing its appearance.  

