However, the remainder must be less than the divisor, so the divisor must be greater than 7.
If the counting number is the divisor, then the remainder is 7, so we can write the division as
\[ 61 = 7 + d \cdot q, \quad \text{where } q \text{ is the quotient and } d > 7 \text{ is the divisor.} \]
Subtracting 7 from both sides, we get
\[ 54 = d \cdot q, \quad \text{where } d > 7 \text{ is the divisor and }q \text{ is the quotient.} \]
Thus, the counting number is a divisor of 54, and the counting number must be greater than 7.
The divisors of 54 are 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 12, 18, 27, 36, 54.
