2. **Calculate the hydrostatic pressure at the inlet pipe**:  
   
   The hydrostatic pressure is the pressure exerted by the water due to its weight.  
   \[
   P_h = \rho g h
   \]
   where:  
   \[
   P_h = \text{hydrostatic pressure (Pa)} \\
   \rho = \text{density of water (kg/m}^3\).
   g = \text{acceleration due to gravity (m/s^2)} \\
   h = \text{depth of the inlet pipe (m)}
   \]

3. **Determine the saturation vapor pressure at 20°C**:  
   
   Caviation occurs when the pressure drops below the saturation vapor pressure of the liquid.  
   
