\]

Substituting these values into the formula:
\[
B = \frac{(10^{-6} \, \text{T} \cdot \text{A}cdot \text{m}cdot \text{C}) \times 100 \, \text{turns} \times 1 \, \text{A}}{2 \times 0.2 \, \text{m}}
\]
\[
B = \frac{10^{-6} \times 100 \times 1}{0.4} \, \text{T}
\]
\[
B = \frac{10^{-4}}{0.4} \, \text{T}
\]
\[
B = 2.5 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{T}
\]

Thus, the magnetic field strength at the center of the circular coil is \(\boxed{2.5 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{T}}\).
